"மாக்குரல்","parts":[{"text":"மாக்குரல்","lemma":"மாக்குரல்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"நொச்சி","parts":[{"text":"நொச்சி","lemma":"நொச்சி","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true},{"words":[{"surface":"போது","parts":[{"text":"போது","lemma":"pōtu","gloss":"flower bud"}],"gloss":"flower bud"},{"surface":"விரி","parts":[{"text":"விரி","lemma":"viri","gloss":"expanding / blooming"}],"gloss":"expanding"},{"surface":"பன்மரன்","parts":[{"text":"பன்மரன்","lemma":"பன்மரன்","gloss":"many trees"}],"gloss":"many trees","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"உள்ளும்","parts":[{"text":"உள்ளும்","lemma":"uḷ","gloss":"even among / within"}],"gloss":"even among"},{"surface":"சிறந்த","parts":[{"text":"சிறந்த","lemma":"ciṟa","gloss":"distinguished / best"}],"gloss":"distinguished"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"காதல்","parts":[{"text":"காதல்","lemma":"kātal","gloss":"beloved / desirable"}],"gloss":"beloved"},{"surface":"நன்மரம்","parts":[{"text":"நன்மரம்","lemma":"நன்மரம்","gloss":"good tree"}],"gloss":"good tree","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"நீ","parts":[{"text":"நீ","lemma":"nī","gloss":"you"}],"gloss":"you"},{"surface":"நிழல்","parts":[{"text":"நிழல்","lemma":"niḻal","gloss":"shade / shelter"}],"gloss":"shade"},{"surface":"திசினே","parts":[{"text":"திசின்","lemma":"ticin","gloss":"second person past suffix"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"clitic"}],"gloss":"you gave"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கடியுடை","parts":[{"text":"கடி","lemma":"kaṭi","gloss":"protection / defense"},{"text":"உடை","lemma":"uṭai","gloss":"having"}],"gloss":"well-guarded"},{"surface":"வியன்நகர்","parts":[{"text":"வியன்","lemma":"viyaṉ","gloss":"spacious / wide"},{"text":"நகர்","lemma":"nakar","gloss":"city / palace"}],"gloss":"spacious city"},{"surface":"காண்வர","parts":[{"text":"காண்","lemma":"kāṇ","gloss":"sight / beauty"},{"text":"வர","lemma":"vara","gloss":"to come / to appear"}],"gloss":"beautifully"},{"surface":"பொலிந்த","parts":[{"text":"பொலிந்த","lemma":"poli","gloss":"shone / was splendid"}],"gloss":"splendid"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"தொடியுடை","parts":[{"text":"தொடி","lemma":"toṭi","gloss":"bangles / armlets"},{"text":"உடை","lemma":"uṭai","gloss":"having"}],"gloss":"wearing bangles"},{"surface":"மகளிர்","parts":[{"text":"மகளிர்","lemma":"makaḷir","gloss":"women"}],"gloss":"women"},{"surface":"அல்குலும்","parts":[{"text":"அல்குல்","lemma":"alkul","gloss":"waist / loins"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"also"}],"gloss":"also on the waists"},{"surface":"கிடத்தி","parts":[{"text":"கிடத்தி","lemma":"kiṭa","gloss":"you lie / rest"}],"gloss":"you lie"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"காப்புடை","parts":[{"text":"காப்பு","lemma":"kāppu","gloss":"protection / guard"},{"text":"உடை","lemma":"uṭai","gloss":"having"}],"gloss":"well-guarded"},{"surface":"புரிசை","parts":[{"text":"புரிசை","lemma":"puricai","gloss":"fort wall / rampart"}],"gloss":"fort wall"},{"surface":"புக்குமாறு","parts":[{"text":"புக்குமாறு","lemma":"புக்குமாறு","gloss":"the way of entering"}],"gloss":"the way of entering","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"அழித்தலின்","parts":[{"text":"அழித்தலின்","lemma":"aḻi","gloss":"because of destroying"}],"gloss":"because of destroying"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஊர்ப்புறம்","parts":[{"text":"ஊர்","lemma":"ūr","gloss":"town"},{"text":"புறம்","lemma":"puṟam","gloss":"back / outside"}],"gloss":"back of the town (not retreating)"},{"surface":"கொடாஅ","parts":[{"text":"கொடாஅ","lemma":"koṭāa","gloss":"not yielding / not showing"}],"gloss":"not yielding"},{"surface":"நெடுந்தகை","parts":[{"text":"நெடும்","lemma":"neṭu","gloss":"great / tall"},{"text":"தகை","lemma":"takai","gloss":"quality / greatness"}],"gloss":"noble hero"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பீடுகெழு","parts":[{"text":"பீடுகெழு","lemma":"பீடுகெழு","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"சென்னிக்","parts":[{"text":"சென்னிக்","lemma":"சென்னிக்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கிழமையும்","parts":[{"text":"கிழமையும்","lemma":"கிழமையும்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"நினதே","parts":[{"text":"நினதே","lemma":"நினதே","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true}],"literal":"Sapphire clustered like dark-bunched nocci, / expanding buds many trees even among distinguished / beloved good tree you shade gave! / Well-guarded spacious city beautifully splendid / wearing bangles women waists also you lie; / well-guarded fort wall the way of entering because of destroying, / back of the town not yielding noble hero's / glorious head's ownership also is yours alone.","translation":"O nocci tree with dark clusters like bunches of sapphires! Among the many trees with blooming buds, you are the most distinguished, beloved, good tree that gave shade. You lie on the loins of the bangle-wearing women who shine beautifully in the well-guarded, spacious city. And because he destroyed the enemy's guarded fort walls by entering them, and never showed his back to the town, the glorious head of that noble hero also belongs to you!","modern":"நீலமணி போன்ற கரிய பூங்கொத்துகளை உடைய நொச்சி மரமே! மலரும் மொட்டுகளைக் கொண்ட பல மரங்களுக்குள்ளும் சிறந்த, அன்பிற்குரிய நல்ல மரமாகிய நீ நிழல் தந்தாய். காவல் மிகுந்த அகன்ற நகரில் அழகுடன் விளங்கும் வளையல் அணிந்த மகளிரின் அல்குல் மீதும் நீ கிடக்கின்றாய். காவல் உடைய மதிலுக்குள் புகுந்து பகைவரை அழித்ததால், தன் ஊருக்குப் புறமுதுகு காட்டாது வீழ்ந்த நெடுந்தகையின் பெருமை பொருந்திய தலையைச் சூடும் உரிமையும் உனக்கே உரியது.","explanation":"The poet Moci Cattanar addresses the nocci (chaste) tree, praising its beauty and its intimate connection with the warriors and women of the town. The poem belongs to the nocci tiṇai (defense of the fortress), and the theme is ceruviṭai vīḻtal (falling in battle). The poet notes that the nocci tree not only provides shade and adorns the waists of beautiful women in times of peace, but also crowns the heads of brave heroes who die defending their fortresses. Since the noble hero died fighting bravely without ever retreating (not showing his back to the town), his glorious head is now adorned with the nocci flowers, giving the tree the ultimate right of ownership over his head. The imagery beautifully contrasts the soft, domestic life of peace with the grim, heroic sacrifice of war, both united by the presence of the nocci tree.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}